1
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:07,250
♪By red walls and a dry well,
my crown gathers dust and frost♪

2
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:11,860
♪With a hoe and a patch of wasteland,
I sow the moonlight♪

3
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:16,120
♪Who says the Cold Palace
holds nothing but tears?♪

4
00:00:16,310 --> 00:00:20,330
♪I choose to fill it with fragrant wine♪

5
00:00:20,670 --> 00:00:22,200
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

6
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:24,730
♪Growing life's simple joys♪

7
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,880
♪Bins full of grain, jars full of wine♪

8
00:00:26,970 --> 00:00:28,760
♪Better than dancing in silks♪

9
00:00:29,420 --> 00:00:30,650
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

10
00:00:30,930 --> 00:00:33,320
♪My heart longs for the world beyond♪

11
00:00:33,690 --> 00:00:35,800
♪Tending a courtyard full of life♪

12
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:40,560
♪Come, share a cup with me♪

13
00:00:40,570 --> 00:00:42,540
(Welcome to Cold Palace Refreshments)

14
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:47,040
=Farm Busily in the Cold Palace=

15
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:48,620
(Based on Hongshu.com's novel
I'm Busy Farming in the Cold Palace)

16
00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:49,650
=Episode 18=

17
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:53,920
Yinshuang, I'm going to bed.

18
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:55,119
Have Jia and Yi guard the grounds.

19
00:00:55,119 --> 00:00:55,479
Yes.

20
00:00:55,479 --> 00:00:56,679
No one is to come in.

21
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:10,439
(Welcome back, host.)

22
00:01:10,599 --> 00:01:12,640
(Current farming points: 8,000.)

23
00:01:12,799 --> 00:01:15,040
(You can upgrade your farm to Level 4.)

24
00:01:15,159 --> 00:01:18,359
Didn't you say points could buy items?

25
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:22,840
I want smallpox treatment methods for
this era.

26
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:24,319
(Danger
Warning! Warning!)

27
00:01:24,599 --> 00:01:27,159
(This will cost all your farming points)

28
00:01:27,359 --> 00:01:29,879
(and all your stored crops.)

29
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:31,359
(Confirm exchange?)

30
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:34,519
Confirm.

31
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:36,880
(Exchanging...)

32
00:01:38,104 --> 00:01:40,460
(Exchanging...)

33
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:42,920
(Exchanging...)

34
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:44,000
(Exchange complete.)

35
00:01:44,359 --> 00:01:46,959
(Transferring smallpox treatment methods
for this era.)

36
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:51,920
(Scarification
Maintain fluid and mineral balance)

37
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:55,467
(Natural pH indicator
Isolate patients)

38
00:01:55,467 --> 00:01:58,390
(Silk protein absorbs impurities)

39
00:01:58,390 --> 00:02:01,640
(Disinfect shared areas with quicklime)

40
00:02:01,719 --> 00:02:04,079
(Adjust transfer speed?)

41
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:06,280
Keep... keep going.

42
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:11,029
(Honeysuckle detoxification
Powdered borneol and talc)

43
00:02:11,029 --> 00:02:14,591
(Purge heat from the upper body
and drain it downward)

44
00:02:14,591 --> 00:02:17,560
(Draw out rashes and pus
Isolate patients)

45
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:18,759
You can't die.

46
00:02:19,199 --> 00:02:20,360
Wait for me to get back.

47
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:23,354
(Powdered borneol and talc)

48
00:02:23,354 --> 00:02:26,161
(Purge heat; draw out rashes and pus)

49
00:02:26,161 --> 00:02:30,840
(Isolate patients; use calamine
Honeysuckle detoxification)

50
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:35,400
Did it work?

51
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:43,719
First, I need to extract penicillin

52
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:47,439
from moldy food.

53
00:02:49,439 --> 00:02:50,960
Culture it by fermentation,

54
00:02:51,479 --> 00:02:52,759
purify with acids and alkalis,

55
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:56,240
then separate it using animal fat.

56
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:57,840
Wait.

57
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:59,800
Where can I get that in this era?

58
00:03:02,439 --> 00:03:03,360
Right!

59
00:03:04,319 --> 00:03:05,560
I think my professor said

60
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:08,639
fresh pomelo peel yields citric acid

61
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:09,919
for use in separation.

62
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:12,759
I planted pomelos!

63
00:03:16,199 --> 00:03:18,319
But it cleared out all my stock.

64
00:03:19,919 --> 00:03:21,000
System!

65
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,400
System, get out here!

66
00:03:22,759 --> 00:03:24,159
You can take everything else,

67
00:03:24,199 --> 00:03:26,120
but give me back my pomelos!

68
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:29,039
(Exchange rules cannot be changed.)

69
00:03:30,039 --> 00:03:30,800
Wait!

70
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:32,680
Can I buy them on credit?

71
00:03:33,159 --> 00:03:35,280
I'll pay you back when I grow more!

72
00:03:36,479 --> 00:03:37,479
(Searching...)

73
00:03:38,319 --> 00:03:40,400
(Sorry. No precedent found.)

74
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,840
There's an epidemic out there!

75
00:03:43,879 --> 00:03:45,199
The emperor's about to die!

76
00:03:45,199 --> 00:03:46,639
Donglan is about to fall!

77
00:03:46,639 --> 00:03:48,000
Who'll buy my crops then?

78
00:03:48,319 --> 00:03:49,520
Then how will you get points?

79
00:03:50,759 --> 00:03:51,560
(Agreed.)

80
00:03:51,639 --> 00:03:54,280
(Interest will be charged at 50%.)

81
00:03:55,199 --> 00:03:56,560
Fine, fine, fine!

82
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:57,400
Give me the pomelos, now!

83
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:58,000
Hand them over!

84
00:03:58,039 --> 00:03:59,159
(Special Loan Agreement)

85
00:03:59,159 --> 00:03:59,919
You greedy merchant.

86
00:03:59,919 --> 00:04:00,919
(Agreement in effect)

87
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:04,560
(Cold Palace)

88
00:04:07,039 --> 00:04:07,879
Yinshuang.

89
00:04:07,879 --> 00:04:09,560
Peel the pomelos.

90
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,120
Yes, my lady.

91
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:14,280
Matron, go to the Cold Palace kitchen

92
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:16,519
and get moldy rice water and vegetables.

93
00:04:16,519 --> 00:04:17,639
Yes, my lady.

94
00:04:17,639 --> 00:04:18,319
Jia.

95
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:19,120
Yes?

96
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:20,240
Bring me a chamber pot.

97
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:20,800
Yes, my lady.

98
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:21,279
Yi.

99
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:23,800
Get some horse manure from the stables.

100
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:24,720
Right away.

101
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:25,920
Wait!

102
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,040
Make sure it's fresh!

103
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:29,160
Hmph.

104
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:54,160
Finest Hetian jade

105
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:55,800
conducts and retains heat.

106
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:57,720
It cost a fortune.

107
00:04:59,519 --> 00:05:00,399
Ji Wujue,

108
00:05:01,879 --> 00:05:03,000
you'd better pay me back.

109
00:05:03,759 --> 00:05:06,759
Mixing pomelo juice with the ferment
creates separate layers.

110
00:05:10,519 --> 00:05:13,720
Human urine is a natural pH indicator.

111
00:05:30,439 --> 00:05:32,879
Silk protein binds impurities.

112
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:54,399
It worked! It worked!

113
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:03,399
Brother.

114
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:05,879
This is all my fault.

115
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:07,680
If it weren't for me...

116
00:06:07,879 --> 00:06:08,959
If you hadn't

117
00:06:09,839 --> 00:06:11,000
always been such a fool,

118
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:12,920
incapable of anything great,

119
00:06:14,079 --> 00:06:15,439
I might have thought

120
00:06:16,199 --> 00:06:17,959
you were an enemy assassin.

121
00:06:18,519 --> 00:06:19,839
They say

122
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:23,560
the dying speak kindly.

123
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:28,199
Why are your words still so cruel?

124
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:30,199
Who says we're dying?

125
00:06:31,879 --> 00:06:33,199
Is there a woman you fancy?

126
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:35,639
Once you're well,

127
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:38,879
I'll arrange your marriage.

128
00:06:39,879 --> 00:06:41,399
One won't be enough.

129
00:06:41,879 --> 00:06:43,319
I want two.

130
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:49,079
How is Prince Rui?

131
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:52,160
Heaven will protect His Highness.

132
00:06:52,399 --> 00:06:53,360
Hear that?

133
00:06:53,879 --> 00:06:55,199
Stop talking

134
00:06:55,279 --> 00:06:56,240
and save your strength.

135
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:57,399
Brother.

136
00:06:58,639 --> 00:06:59,959
Do you remember

137
00:07:00,839 --> 00:07:04,639
when our eldest brother locked you in
the library?

138
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:07,000
I stole Father's key

139
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,959
and rushed to the dog hole to save you.

140
00:07:09,519 --> 00:07:10,639
But then

141
00:07:11,759 --> 00:07:13,279
I got stuck,

142
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:16,040
wailing for the whole palace to hear.

143
00:07:18,639 --> 00:07:20,040
That was so long ago.

144
00:07:20,959 --> 00:07:21,920
Why bring it up?

145
00:07:22,639 --> 00:07:23,439
But

146
00:07:24,279 --> 00:07:25,839
I told you then

147
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:27,160
that hole

148
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,120
was far too small for you.

149
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:30,800
But you

150
00:07:32,079 --> 00:07:34,279
still got me out.

151
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:37,600
They mocked my mother for being a
singer.

152
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:41,959
You always looked after me.

153
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:45,759
You always clung to me like glue.

154
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:49,639
I resented you once, you know.

155
00:07:51,759 --> 00:07:53,600
You learned how to rule,

156
00:07:53,839 --> 00:07:57,680
while I could only learn how to serve.

157
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:00,319
Why were you born the crown prince,

158
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:02,639
with an empress for a mother?

159
00:08:03,839 --> 00:08:05,199
But the night she died,

160
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:08,680
though you were trembling with fear,

161
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:12,399
you kept vigil all night

162
00:08:13,959 --> 00:08:15,000
in my place.

163
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:18,839
Because you said

164
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:24,160
an emperor must not cry.

165
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:34,799
Who let you in?

166
00:08:34,919 --> 00:08:36,080
If I hadn't come when I did,

167
00:08:36,279 --> 00:08:37,320
he'd have started to stink!

168
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:38,320
Brother.

169
00:08:39,639 --> 00:08:40,600
My mother

170
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:43,679
has come for me.

171
00:08:46,639 --> 00:08:47,600
Do you want to die?

172
00:08:47,879 --> 00:08:49,279
Get out!

173
00:08:49,279 --> 00:08:53,120
I can see Father dancing too!

174
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:53,919
See?

175
00:08:54,519 --> 00:08:56,080
He's already delirious.

176
00:08:57,879 --> 00:08:59,080
Lu Yunluo.

177
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,480
This isn't a chill.

178
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,600
It's smallpox.

179
00:09:05,039 --> 00:09:06,039
I know.

180
00:09:07,039 --> 00:09:08,320
Then why are you here?

181
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:10,919
Ji Wujue.

182
00:09:11,799 --> 00:09:12,759
Do you trust me?

183
00:09:14,759 --> 00:09:17,080
My lady, the sun is scorching.

184
00:09:17,279 --> 00:09:18,840
Will it really rain tomorrow?

185
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:20,679
It will if I say it will.

186
00:09:22,879 --> 00:09:24,159
You really didn't lie to me.

187
00:09:40,879 --> 00:09:42,879
Your Majesty, what now?

188
00:09:45,039 --> 00:09:45,840
We wait.

189
00:09:49,879 --> 00:09:51,039
(If this time,)

190
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:53,279
(we both survive...)

191
00:09:58,639 --> 00:09:59,679
Your Majesty.

192
00:09:59,679 --> 00:10:01,279
If the Emperor truly has the disease,

193
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:02,960
you mustn't risk your health.

194
00:10:10,159 --> 00:10:11,159
Cao Zhongquan.

195
00:10:11,159 --> 00:10:12,120
Yes, Your Majesty.

196
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:15,120
I hear His Majesty is unwell.

197
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:17,159
What did the Medical Office say?

198
00:10:17,879 --> 00:10:18,960
Your Majesty,

199
00:10:19,159 --> 00:10:21,440
they say it's from overwork.

200
00:10:21,519 --> 00:10:23,559
It's merely a chill.

201
00:10:23,679 --> 00:10:25,440
A mere chill

202
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,919
needs Imperial Guards?

203
00:10:28,879 --> 00:10:30,480
So he's guarding against me?

204
00:10:34,879 --> 00:10:35,840
Wujue.

205
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:37,679
I came especially to see you.

206
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,399
Thank you for your concern, Mother.

207
00:10:42,399 --> 00:10:43,440
I'm quite well.

208
00:10:45,799 --> 00:10:48,279
My child, look at you.

209
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:50,000
You've had me so worried.

210
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,639
If you're so worried,

211
00:10:55,279 --> 00:10:57,120
why not come inside?

212
00:11:07,759 --> 00:11:10,840
Then I won't disturb your recovery.

213
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:13,559
Rest well, Your Majesty.

214
00:11:21,759 --> 00:11:22,679
Visiting the sick?

215
00:11:23,480 --> 00:11:24,279
Hmph.

216
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:26,159
I think

217
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:29,600
you're just waiting for me to die.

218
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:56,630
♪By red walls and a dry well,
my crown gathers dust and frost♪

219
00:11:57,020 --> 00:12:01,240
♪With a hoe and a patch of wasteland,
I sow the moonlight♪

220
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:05,460
♪Who says the Cold Palace
holds nothing but tears?♪

221
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:09,710
♪I choose to fill it with fragrant wine♪

222
00:12:10,050 --> 00:12:14,110
♪Cool dew, starry nights,
wheat sprouts in my hands♪

223
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:18,360
♪I shape fields, not painted brows,
and fill them with hope♪

224
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:22,170
♪Gold and silver bloom from the soil♪

225
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:27,320
♪I smile as the world storms on♪

226
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:31,130
♪No finery to rival spring♪

227
00:12:31,310 --> 00:12:35,610
♪All I wish for are waves of green♪

228
00:12:38,020 --> 00:12:39,770
♪Where is beauty found?♪

229
00:12:39,950 --> 00:12:44,380
♪Just lift your eyes and see♪

230
00:12:44,940 --> 00:12:46,510
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

231
00:12:46,530 --> 00:12:49,000
♪Growing life's simple joys♪

232
00:12:49,070 --> 00:12:51,150
♪Bins full of grain, jars full of wine♪

233
00:12:51,310 --> 00:12:53,080
♪Better than dancing in silks♪

234
00:12:53,690 --> 00:12:54,960
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

235
00:12:55,190 --> 00:12:57,590
♪My heart longs for the world beyond♪

236
00:12:57,830 --> 00:13:00,130
♪Tending a courtyard full of life♪

237
00:13:00,410 --> 00:13:04,730
♪Come, share a cup with me♪
